    topic: "Sport",
    prompt: "Does watching sport encourage people to play it?",
    sample: "It encourages a particular fantasy, which only sometimes becomes a habit. After a tournament you see more people on courts and in parks, and most of them have gone within a month. Watching does teach the eye: you recognise a good pass, and you may want that feeling in your own body. It can also do the opposite. Elite sport is so far from a beginner's competence that some viewers conclude the activity belongs to other people. The link is strongest when the watched sport is easy to start locally, at a low price, without needing the body you saw on television. Inspiration is cheap. A nearby pitch with the lights on is the actual policy.",
