    topic: "Food",
    prompt: "Should people try to eat food that is produced locally?",
    sample: "Local food can be fresher and can keep money in a nearby economy, but 'local' is not a synonym for ethical or even for low emissions. A heated greenhouse next door may cost the climate more than a ship bringing grain from a suitable climate. I would rather people learn a few distinctions than adopt a sticker. Seasonal fruit, shorter chains for food that spoils, and less obsession with having every ingredient in every month: those are sensible. Coffee, spices and a lot of staple trade are not local for most of us, and pretending otherwise is a hobby. Eat nearby when the reason is real. Do not make a moral identity out of a radius.",
