    topic: "Food",
    prompt: "Is cooking becoming a lost skill?",
    sample: "It is becoming an uneven skill, which is more serious than it being rare. Some young adults cook elaborate meals as a hobby and cannot produce a cheap, ordinary supper on a Wednesday. Others never saw the ordinary supper either, because both parents worked and the meal arrived in a box. Recipes on a phone mean the information is not lost. The habit is. A skill survives when it is used on dull days, not when it is performed for guests. Schools could teach three reliable dishes and the idea of leftovers, which would matter more than another competition. Cooking will not vanish. It may become something a confident minority do while everyone else reheats.",
