    sample: "The support has to be ordinary, or it will not scale. Pensions that keep people out of poverty, housing that does not require stairs they can no longer manage, and clinics that are near the bus: these are less photogenic than an innovation conference and more useful. Families still do a great deal of care, and they will crack if policy assumes they can do all of it. Paid carers need wages that make the job survivable, or the system is a speech about respect sitting on underpaid labour. Older people are not a single burden. Many work, volunteer and look after grandchildren. The design fails when it notices them only after they are already in crisis.",
