    sample: "They bring memory of how a problem was solved the last time, including the solution that failed and should not be repeated with a new name. That kind of judgement is hard to hire in a graduate. Older staff are often calmer with an angry customer and less tempted to treat every delay as a crisis. The lazy view is that they resist change. Some do. Others have watched enough fashions to ask whether the new system actually works, which is a service if the room can bear it. A workplace that pushes them out at the first chance loses continuity. One that refuses to let younger staff lead loses the future. The mix is the point.",
